Question: Did Entero Therapeutics (formerly First Wave BioPharma) stop any phase 2 trials without posting results, and what reasons did it give?

Snapshot date: 2026-11-05
Research notes: Stopped at the cap of 3 research rounds.

Findings:
[{"lane": "trials", "round": 1, "brief": "Investigate the registry records for three terminated phase 2 trials sponsored by Entero Therapeutics (formerly First Wave BioPharma or AzurRx SAS): NCT03521232 (niclosamide enemas for ulcerative proctitis, primary completion Sept 2022), NCT04839575 (latiglutenase for celiac disease in T1D, primary completion Dec 2022), and NCT04243551 (latiglutenase for symptomatic celiac disease, primary completion Oct 2023). Verify their final enrollment numbers, registry statuses, exact dates, stated termination reasons, and whether results have been posted or are overdue on ClinicalTrials.gov.", "findings": [{"claim": "Trial NCT03521232 is terminated, with an enrollment of 27 patients, start date May 15, 2018, primary completion September 19, 2022, and completion date October 4, 2022.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT03521232"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Live registry check confirms snapshot."}, {"claim": "Trial NCT03521232 stated why_stopped reason is 'Covid-19' (categorized as other).", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT03521232"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Live registry check confirms snapshot."}, {"claim": "Trial NCT03521232 has results_posted as false, results_due_date September 19, 2023, and is overdue with days_late at 1143.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT03521232"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Live registry check confirms snapshot."}, {"claim": "Trial NCT04839575 is terminated, with an enrollment of 13 patients, start date April 6, 2021, primary completion December 19, 2022, and completion date December 19, 2022.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT04839575"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Live registry check confirms snapshot."}, {"claim": "Trial NCT04839575 stated why_stopped reason is 'Covid-19 interruptions and enrollment challenges' (categorized as enrollment).", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT04839575"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Live registry check confirms snapshot."}, {"claim": "Trial NCT04839575 has results_posted as false, results_due_date December 19, 2023, and is overdue with days_late at 1052.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT04839575"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Live registry check confirms snapshot."}, {"claim": "Trial NCT04243551 is terminated, with an enrollment of 83 patients, start date November 1, 2019, primary completion October 16, 2023, and completion date October 31, 2023.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT04243551"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Live registry check confirms snapshot."}, {"claim": "Trial NCT04243551 stated why_stopped reason is 'Due to low enrollment related to Covid.' (categorized as enrollment).", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT04243551"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Live registry check confirms snapshot."}, {"claim": "Trial NCT04243551 has results_posted as false, results_due_date October 15, 2024, and is overdue with days_late at 751.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT04243551"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Live registry check confirms snapshot."}, {"claim": "Niclosamide has an FDA application (NDA018669 under Niclocide, marked as Discontinued), but no approval found for this formulation/indication directly under Entero Therapeutics.", "evidence_ids": ["fda:NDA018669"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Drugs@FDA check."}, {"claim": "Latiglutenase has no FDA approval or application listed in Drugs@FDA.", "evidence_ids": ["fda:none:latiglutenase"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Drugs@FDA check."}], "gaps": []}, {"lane": "disclosures", "round": 1, "brief": "Search SEC filings for Entero Therapeutics (formerly First Wave BioPharma, CIK 0001604191) to see what was disclosed to investors regarding the termination of three phase 2 trials: NCT03521232 (niclosamide enemas, stopped around September to November 2022), NCT04839575 (latiglutenase, stopped around December 2022), and NCT04243551 (latiglutenase, stopped around October to December 2023). Review 8-K filings within 120 days of their primary completion or termination dates to see how the clinical pipeline changes were explained to the public.", "findings": [{"claim": "For the niclosamide enemas trial NCT03521232 (stopped around September to November 2022), Form 8-K filings around October and November 2022 mention that the company is advancing multiple programs involving niclosamide, but do not specifically name trial NCT03521232 or disclose its termination.", "evidence_ids": ["sec:0001104659-22-107922", "sec:0001104659-22-121003", "sec:0001104659-22-122476"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Filings from October and November 2022 discuss niclosamide progress broadly rather than trial-specific discontinuation."}, {"claim": "For the latiglutenase trial NCT04839575 (stopped around December 2022), no Form 8-K filings directly addressing the termination of this specific trial within 120 days of its completion or stop date were returned in the snapshot filings for this NCT ID.", "evidence_ids": ["sec:0001104659-24-084206", "sec:0001104659-24-079101", "sec:0001104659-24-092491"], "confidence": "medium", "notes": "Later filings in mid-2024 discuss Phase 3 planning and trial design updates for latiglutenase, but not the specific 2022 trial stop."}, {"claim": "For the latiglutenase trial NCT04243551 (stopped around October to December 2023), Form 8-K filings in December 2023 announced a business combination with ImmunogenX and the expansion of the clinical pipeline to include Phase 3-ready latiglutenase for celiac disease, as well as a streamlining of the clinical pipeline involving the niclosamide IBD program.", "evidence_ids": ["sec:0001104659-23-126593", "sec:0001104659-23-129426"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Announced strategic pipeline updates and business combination without explicitly detailing the individual trial termination for NCT04243551."}], "gaps": []}, {"lane": "publications", "round": 1, "brief": "Search PubMed and Europe PMC for any journal publications reporting findings or results from three terminated phase 2 trials sponsored by Entero Therapeutics (formerly First Wave BioPharma): NCT03521232, NCT04839575, and NCT04243551. Check if any results papers or abstracts were published, even if summary results were not posted on ClinicalTrials.gov, and outline their findings.", "findings": [{"claim": "For NCT03521232, find_publications returned no articles directly reporting trial results; all linked items are europepmc_mention hits (PMIDs 31511071, 36297645, 36735625) which are merely drug/topic mentions rather than trial outcome papers.", "evidence_ids": ["pubmed:31511071", "pubmed:36297645", "pubmed:36735625"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Europe PMC text-mining mentions, not trial results publications."}, {"claim": "For NCT04839575, find_publications returned no articles directly reporting trial results; all linked items are europepmc_mention hits (PMIDs 38698821, 39493330, 39862215, 41595566) which are review articles or general mentions.", "evidence_ids": ["pubmed:38698821", "pubmed:39493330", "pubmed:39862215", "pubmed:41595566"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Europe PMC text-mining mentions, not trial results publications."}, {"claim": "For NCT04243551, find_publications returned no articles directly reporting trial results; all linked items are europepmc_mention hits (PMIDs 38140342, 38698821, 39493330, 39941971, 39862215) which are review articles or general mentions.", "evidence_ids": ["pubmed:38140342", "pubmed:38698821", "pubmed:39493330", "pubmed:39941971", "pubmed:39862215"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Europe PMC text-mining mentions, not trial results publications."}], "gaps": ["No dedicated peer-reviewed trial results publications were found in PubMed or Europe PMC for NCT03521232, NCT04839575, or NCT04243551. Results may exist in conference abstracts, company press releases, or clinical trial registry entries which these sources do not cover."]}, {"lane": "disclosures", "round": 2, "brief": "Search SEC 10-K and 10-Q filings for Entero Therapeutics / First Wave BioPharma (CIK 0001604191) for Fiscal Years 2022, 2023, and Q1 2024. Look for specific disclosures or discussions in the Business and MD&A sections explaining the discontinuation, suspension, or termination of trials NCT03521232 (niclosamide enemas for ulcerative proctitis), NCT04839575 (latiglutenase in T1D), and NCT04243551 (latiglutenase for symptomatic celiac disease).\n\n(Gap to close: Sponsor CIK matched but key Phase 2 trial discontinuations were not found in 8-K filings; 10-K and 10-Q filings during the relevant periods were not analyzed.)", "findings": [{"claim": "Ran out of turns. Records gathered: ctgov:NCT03521232, ctgov:NCT03746483, ctgov:NCT04243551, ctgov:NCT04375878, ctgov:NCT04436458, ctgov:NCT04542434, ctgov:NCT04839575, ctgov:NCT04858425, ctgov:NCT05719311, sec:0001104659-22-107922, sec:0001104659-22-121003, sec:0001104659-22-122476, sec:0001104659-23-126593, sec:0001104659-23-129426, sec:0001104659-24-079101, sec:0001104659-24-084206, sec:0001104659-24-092491, sql:4c84c5b0, sql:4e3aad35.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT03521232", "ctgov:NCT03746483", "ctgov:NCT04243551", "ctgov:NCT04375878", "ctgov:NCT04436458", "ctgov:NCT04542434", "ctgov:NCT04839575", "ctgov:NCT04858425", "ctgov:NCT05719311", "sec:0001104659-22-107922", "sec:0001104659-22-121003", "sec:0001104659-22-122476", "sec:0001104659-23-126593", "sec:0001104659-23-129426", "sec:0001104659-24-079101", "sec:0001104659-24-084206", "sec:0001104659-24-092491", "sql:4c84c5b0", "sql:4e3aad35"], "confidence": "low", "notes": ""}], "gaps": ["Researcher hit the 8-turn cap before finishing: Search SEC 10-K and 10-Q filings for Entero Therapeutics / First Wave BioPharma (CIK 0001604191) for Fiscal Years 2022, 2023, and Q1 2024. Look for specific disclosures or discussions in the Business "]}, {"lane": "disclosures", "round": 3, "brief": "Search SEC 10-K and 10-Q filings for Entero Therapeutics, formerly First Wave BioPharma, CIK 0001604191, for Fiscal Years 2022, 2023, and Q1 2024. Retrieve and analyze disclosures explaining the termination, discontinuation, or pipeline streamlining of trials NCT03521232 (niclosamide enemas), NCT04839575 (latiglutenase in T1D), and NCT04243551 (latiglutenase for celiac disease).\n\n(Gap to close: Specific disclosures regarding Phase 2 trial terminations for NCT03521232, NCT04839575, and NCT04243551 are missing from SEC annual and quarterly filings because the researcher ran out of turns.)", "findings": [{"claim": "First Wave BioPharma announced a streamlining of its clinical pipeline on December 27, 2023, via an 8-K filing, including a non-binding term sheet to sell the Niclosamide IBD program, while pivoting to advance latiglutenase for celiac disease.", "evidence_ids": ["sec:0001104659-23-129426"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Mentions pipeline streamlining and the Niclosamide IBD program sale."}, {"claim": "First Wave BioPharma announced entry into a term sheet for a business combination with ImmunogenX on December 18, 2023, expanding its pipeline to include the Phase 3-ready latiglutenase for celiac disease.", "evidence_ids": ["sec:0001104659-23-126593"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Covers acquisition/integration of latiglutenase program."}, {"claim": "Entero Therapeutics (formerly First Wave BioPharma) disclosed in July 2024 filing updates regarding latiglutenase Phase 3 trial design plans, seeking FDA approval to change cohorts from three to two (1200 mg and placebo).", "evidence_ids": ["sec:0001104659-24-084206"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Details trial design adjustments for latiglutenase."}], "gaps": ["Specific 10-K and 10-Q filing text excerpts for FY 2022, 2023, and Q1 2024 regarding NCT03521232, NCT04839575, and NCT04243551 could not be fully extracted via automated text queries due to SEC tool connection constraints."]}]

